{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Observations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Observations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Semi-Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Semi-Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Ultra_Fast_if_you_have_like_20_sec_left)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Ultra Fast if you have like 20 sec left)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/0856042a755ebc88c0261897b7fad311209d9e99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = |\\lfloor x \\rfloor| - |\\lfloor 1 - x \\rfloor|\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" /> is symmetric about which of the following? (Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e138bab3c3d0fbf7980edaab5a68418b395c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\text{the }y\\text{-axis}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\text{the line }x = 1\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\text{the origin}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\text{ the point }\\left(\\dfrac12, 0\\right)\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{the point }(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"808\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Observations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Observations)\">Solution 1 (Observations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Observations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e429798617e9a1f670e956592cb0516f378db114.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1-x)=|\\lfloor 1-x\\rfloor|-|\\lfloor x\\rfloor|=-f(x),\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"18\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a023dd7944450095e37b8e6d91015dbd6118661c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\left(\\frac12+x\\right)=-f\\left(\\frac12-x\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"212\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>This means that the graph is symmetric about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8eda09722451242d2e33472a6fa54651615457e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\text{ the point }\\left(\\dfrac12, 0\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"186\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Graphing)\">Solution 2 (Graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/93527e395fe826a6b2a84403313f1095db389fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1=|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4d4b1c815633cf69ce37536ddce77fa7d7d35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2=|\\lfloor 1 - x \\rfloor|=|\\lfloor -(x-1) \\rfloor|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" /> Note that the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0320ab2ddd4939f9072e5316fe8888b0cddee319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> is a reflection of the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae250d1bdd46e5677f27edcf5efb34587b6fc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis, followed by a translation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit to the right.\n</p><p>The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae250d1bdd46e5677f27edcf5efb34587b6fc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> is shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df033d486d401ca1bed7c55adb9ece6814710acb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(250);   int xMin = -10; int xMax = 10; int yMin = -10; int yMax = 10;  //Draws the horizontal gridlines void horizontalLines() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((xMin,i)--(xMax,i), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the vertical gridlines void verticalLines() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,yMin)--(i,yMax), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the horizontal ticks void horizontalTicks() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((-3/16,i)--(3/16,i), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws the vertical ticks void verticalTicks() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,-3/16)--(i,3/16), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws and labels coordinate axes void drawLabelAxes() { \tdraw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tdraw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tlabel(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); \tlabel(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2)); }  horizontalLines(); verticalLines(); horizontalTicks(); verticalTicks(); drawLabelAxes();  path P[], Q[]; for (int i = 0; i &lt; 9; ++i) {     P[i] = (i,i)--(i+1,i);     Q[i] = (-i,i+1)--(-i-1,i+1); } draw(P^^Q,red+linewidth(1.25)); for (int i = 0; i &lt; 9; ++i) {     dot((i,i),red+linewidth(4));     dot((i+1,i),red+linewidth(0.7),UnFill);     dot((-i-1,i+1),red+linewidth(4));     dot((-i,i+1),red+linewidth(0.7),UnFill); } [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"418\" />\nThe graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0320ab2ddd4939f9072e5316fe8888b0cddee319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> is shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7efea0e5b8aa776350e2378f47e4a9de972ac5b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(250);   int xMin = -10; int xMax = 10; int yMin = -10; int yMax = 10;  //Draws the horizontal gridlines void horizontalLines() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((xMin,i)--(xMax,i), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the vertical gridlines void verticalLines() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,yMin)--(i,yMax), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the horizontal ticks void horizontalTicks() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((-3/16,i)--(3/16,i), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws the vertical ticks void verticalTicks() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,-3/16)--(i,3/16), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws and labels coordinate axes void drawLabelAxes() { \tdraw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tdraw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tlabel(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); \tlabel(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2)); }  horizontalLines(); verticalLines(); horizontalTicks(); verticalTicks(); drawLabelAxes();  path P[], Q[]; for (int i = 0; i &lt; 9; ++i) {     P[i] = (i,i)--(i+1,i);     Q[i] = (-i,i+1)--(-i-1,i+1); } draw(P^^Q,heavygreen+linewidth(1.25)); for (int i = 0; i &lt; 9; ++i) {     dot((i,i),heavygreen+linewidth(0.7),UnFill);     dot((i+1,i),heavygreen+linewidth(4));     dot((-i-1,i+1),heavygreen+linewidth(0.7),UnFill);     dot((-i,i+1),heavygreen+linewidth(4)); } [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"418\" />\nThe graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55fb68ab4fc74f52fdf4c7352fcbe1863a87b50d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=y_1-y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> is shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738c5fa07b67319af9f1a6bd017f68e65642bfd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(250);   int xMin = -10; int xMax = 10; int yMin = -10; int yMax = 10;  //Draws the horizontal gridlines void horizontalLines() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((xMin,i)--(xMax,i), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the vertical gridlines void verticalLines() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,yMin)--(i,yMax), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the horizontal ticks void horizontalTicks() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((-3/16,i)--(3/16,i), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws the vertical ticks void verticalTicks() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,-3/16)--(i,3/16), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws and labels coordinate axes void drawLabelAxes() { \tdraw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tdraw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tlabel(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); \tlabel(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2)); }  horizontalLines(); verticalLines(); horizontalTicks(); verticalTicks(); drawLabelAxes();  draw((-10,0)--(10,0),mediumblue+linewidth(1.25),&quot;$y=|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|$&quot;); for (int i = 0; i &gt; -10; --i) {     dot((i,-1),mediumblue+linewidth(4)); } for (int i = 1; i &lt; 10; ++i) {     dot((i,1),mediumblue+linewidth(4)); } for (int i = -9; i &lt; 10; ++i) {     dot((i,0),mediumblue+linewidth(0.7),UnFill); } [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"418\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is symmetric about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56391416ff85c090610a7e0274688fa068a20e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\text{ the point }\\left(\\dfrac12, 0\\right)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"191\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Casework)\">Solution 3 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5de01a97e73f9cd6fd0020787398d81801dd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c3ab03cadda6b8a63ee65aa0e0ede7ab2646c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{Z},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> note that:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/828fee80b3017faa2315f43125bce75e44e91cca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x+n \\rfloor = \\lfloor x \\rfloor + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49dc38f38c7239579798c7f65be122288f25135a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil x+n \\rceil = \\lceil x \\rceil + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0e0fff26fadf874b4dfcbb4910d00326eb4e5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor -x \\rfloor = -\\lceil x \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3dd2710e6fe4293e40e7af56e3992bd1e175a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil x \\rceil - \\lfloor x \\rfloor = \\begin{cases} 0 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x\\in\\mathbb{Z} \\\\  1 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x\\not\\in\\mathbb{Z} \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"205\" height=\"55\" /></li>\n</ol>\n<p>We rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54d27a19f0d78ffe02dce0c6707631ddcde8c94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(x) &amp;= |\\lfloor x \\rfloor| - |\\lfloor 1 - x \\rfloor| \\\\ &amp;= |\\lfloor x \\rfloor| - |-\\lceil x - 1 \\rceil| \\\\ &amp;= |\\lfloor x \\rfloor| - |-\\lceil x \\rceil + 1|. \\end{align*}\" width=\"211\" height=\"68\" />\nWe apply casework to the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c1222c5ec2df9ebdb97a75b04316a1641c5d070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x:$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70cf30533ad4fc8617b2f79b4fbb572a8f7a6d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{Z}^-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /></li><p>\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0af9980c75c474c6f7a75f7512784270025ebf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=-x-(-x+1)=-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /></li><p>\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb1f96c3e49671e50d4564f773dff154f8dbabd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0-1=-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec797c993e864efb44d64b0f7ccf70c27ff3408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{Z}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /></li><p>\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/55409f27e72bc7950b7136311459ecb3cb4cbfbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x-(x-1)=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce03143052f6301e8efe6f60c79fa0da505d742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\not\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /></li><p>\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09c98d7d9d48e2992e20b5ba1c6ea21424a9b7f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=-\\lfloor x \\rfloor - (-\\lceil x\\rceil+1)=(\\lceil x \\rceil - \\lfloor x \\rfloor)-1=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"394\" height=\"20\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce03143052f6301e8efe6f60c79fa0da505d742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\not\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128206b7583760e7ef76e802861294c334f7ca2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /></li><p>\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8294605125a921bdfb8441cd07a62bbf352e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0-0=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce03143052f6301e8efe6f60c79fa0da505d742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\not\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /></li><p>\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c1b5d8057fe6763c5b1082b007747e102264d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\lfloor x \\rfloor - (\\lceil x\\rceil-1)=(\\lfloor x \\rfloor - \\lceil x \\rceil)+1=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"366\" height=\"20\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>Together, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b8c5fedd06ded6f0c79f1f689e400d950b2419d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=\\begin{cases} -1 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x\\in\\mathbb{Z}^{-}\\cup\\{0\\} \\\\  1 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x\\in\\mathbb{Z}^{+} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x\\not\\in\\mathbb{Z} \\end{cases},\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"74\" />\nso the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is symmetric about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56391416ff85c090610a7e0274688fa068a20e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\text{ the point }\\left(\\dfrac12, 0\\right)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"191\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we can eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0010c47708ba62a22ba5c3438fdeefd12fc592c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}, \\textbf{(B)}, \\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> once we finish with Case 3. This leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4feb78447beef6c93631b0912fb24e7936b6dad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Casework)\">Solution 4 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/3094af652c0d9a81d3920e4110cbcaa604604db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c7e2279a6dd7e250c2f4a30cdb74b2e5c0ab06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\in \\Bbb Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/89756bcf5865b9e1ec705bc467a64372339d1db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\in \\left[ 0 , 1 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the integer part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the decimal part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 1</b>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d8f4a1eabd2b788f4a469655f1861619179f016.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f \\left( x \\right) &amp; = \\left| \\lfloor x \\rfloor \\right| - \\left| \\lfloor 1 - x \\rfloor \\right| \\\\ &amp; = | a | - | 1 - a | \\\\ &amp; = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} a - \\left( a - 1 \\right) &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\in \\Bbb Z \\mbox{ and } a \\geq 1 \\\\ -1 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a = 0 \\\\ - a - \\left( 1 - a \\right) &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\in \\Bbb Z \\mbox{ and } a \\leq -1 \\end{array} \\right. \\\\ &amp; = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} 1 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\in \\Bbb Z \\mbox{ and } a \\geq 1 \\\\ -1 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a = 0 \\\\ -1 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\in \\Bbb Z \\mbox{ and } a \\leq -1 \\end{array} \\right. \\\\ &amp; = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} 1 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\in \\Bbb Z \\mbox{ and } a \\geq 1 \\\\ -1 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\in \\Bbb Z \\mbox{ and } a \\leq 0 \\end{array} \\right. \\end{align*}\" width=\"362\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 2</b>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d09016ae7d4bb0ccd869b43b3da544e9bacc08e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f698b6aad7ed95ea1eb1a99cf326130e8bb79bda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f \\left( x \\right) &amp; = \\left| \\lfloor x \\rfloor \\right| - \\left| \\lfloor 1 - x \\rfloor \\right| \\\\ &amp; = | a | - | \\lfloor 1 - a - b \\rfloor | \\\\ &amp; = | a | - | \\lfloor - a + \\left( 1 - b \\right) \\rfloor | \\\\ &amp; = | a | - | - a | \\\\ &amp; = 0 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"227\" height=\"113\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de209f4e2cda26ce5e32c9548d1a1f7855680305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( x \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> is symmetric through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81290033b07ee2c7c6feab2c0ffc2b308d6b490a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac{1}{2} , 0 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8eda09722451242d2e33472a6fa54651615457e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\text{ the point }\\left(\\dfrac12, 0\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"186\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Semi-Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Semi-Fakesolve)\">Solution 5 (Semi-Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Semi-Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9875d1206cca4b1774332e92d17f21163781407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\mathbb{Z},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> making the equation equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c77c1a7912423b1bcb52dcec5d504714824441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = |x|-|1-x|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> We consider the cases when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb026c33f0083e9cee8f8e8b067216a136a27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in (-\\infty, 0), 0, 1, (1, \\infty).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b5366742c167cb157243f81caa0a807532152eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in (-\\infty, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35dc848f2273c12cc13e7a3ad41eb2f2d7b8e3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| = -x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba716c6f7bd6bb21eb31ae1388df23f1f1a39051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|1-x| = 1-x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91a6d81a27519818466525bc6dc1c53cc953116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = -x - (1-x) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, we trivially get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340cac2be385d86e901edb5662ec8113655c1494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. \n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae3dc405e5c8e8e826ca49c4e9fc69df50139c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in (1, \\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f588d481899a45ef11b72260eb17dd1068b6e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3794e0b94ddd6419304dbb60691df86843d90b81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|1-x| = x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f600ec41cf6e72a2ebfefec3c4ce3788f48beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x-(x-1)= 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSince, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478afb215aee9205b34e9dcd5f2b59b3ba736d2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\mathbb{Z} \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/1386b884ad27ff727e59e63008b87ccb451d56d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)  =-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/085c473a80487b619333642d38a96dce88029eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\mathbb{Z} \\geq 1, f(x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />, we can conclude that it is symmetric across the coordinate pair \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df0a9a3fbb513a77a083e00a955e242ac1cdcc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{0 + 1}{2}, \\frac{-1 + 1}{2}\\right) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 0\\right)},\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"54\" />\nthe midpoint of the \"endpoints\" of these line segments. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034d1ba8ffbda60c17eef1d51271fe6b02ca7308.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(250); //Credit to MRENTHUSIASM  int xMin = -10; int xMax = 10; int yMin = -10; int yMax = 10;  //Draws the horizontal gridlines void horizontalLines() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((xMin,i)--(xMax,i), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the vertical gridlines void verticalLines() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,yMin)--(i,yMax), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the horizontal ticks void horizontalTicks() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((-3/16,i)--(3/16,i), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws the vertical ticks void verticalTicks() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,-3/16)--(i,3/16), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws and labels coordinate axes void drawLabelAxes() { \tdraw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tdraw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); \tlabel(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); \tlabel(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2)); }  horizontalLines(); verticalLines(); horizontalTicks(); verticalTicks(); drawLabelAxes();  for (int i = 0; i &gt; -10; --i) {     dot((i,-1),mediumblue+linewidth(4)); } for (int i = 1; i &lt; 10; ++i) {     dot((i,1),mediumblue+linewidth(4)); }  [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"418\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Just considering the integers is never a good idea when dealing with any function, especially one with floor functions. However, after dealing with the case \"when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073924a18f7aa1dd1bd375e11465b2c44c4fd6da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />\", it becomes apparent that the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is symmetric about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2ff20448834be77dc325234211669d2b44d35aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, or more specifically, the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f7208587a39f48d856d64d77e866dd5f76da44be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 0\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"66\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Ultra_Fast_if_you_have_like_20_sec_left.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Ultra_Fast_if_you_have_like_20_sec_left)\">Solution 6 (Ultra Fast if you have like 20 sec left)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Ultra Fast if you have like 20 sec left)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take some simple values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Here we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b6eaefb97a3aeaf94356563131dea34d0fcb221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2,-1,0,1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366d71be5077bf41dc26fb89802d4c794aaa1dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1,-1,-1,1,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" /> respectively. We easily see that choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c4826cbaf7b06a33f9c0c3f675776bac762e693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> is already false, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8eda09722451242d2e33472a6fa54651615457e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\text{ the point }\\left(\\dfrac12, 0\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"186\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p><p>~TheRealMee\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RpxlZJRiSjk\">https://youtu.be/RpxlZJRiSjk</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A\">2021 Fall AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"